From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): switch a running Claude session to another
 provider

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

A session's provider was fixed at creation, so moving a conversation to
another Claude account, or between a subscription and Databricks, meant
starting over.

POST /v1/sessions/{id}/provider takes a providers: entry name (or null for
the host default). The provider lives in the runner's environment, so the
server saves it and restarts the runner: at once when every session on that
runner is idle, otherwise when their turns end, so a turn or a question
waiting on the user is never cut off. A claude-native session's terminal
comes back on the new provider and resumes the conversation; a claude-sdk
session resumes on its next message.

Claude keeps the conversation in its config directory, so a session can only
move between providers that share one. The host provider listing now reports
an opaque switch_group per row (a hash of that directory, never the path):
token accounts and gateway providers share the host's directory, while an
account with its own config_dir keeps its own. The server checks the target
on the host (configured, signed in, same group) before saving anything.
Switching is owner-only, since it decides which of the host owner's
accounts pays, and limited to Claude harnesses for now.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
